  "articleBody": "Thinking about marble tile? It's a gorgeous choice, but there are a few things you'll want to mull over to make sure it's the right fit for your space and lifestyle. First, think about maintenance. Marble is porous, so it needs a bit more TLC than ceramic or porcelain. It's more prone to staining and etching from acidic liquids, so spills need quick cleanup. Next, consider where it's going. Is it for a high-traffic area, a shower, or a heated floor? This will influence the marble's thickness, finish, and the setting materials your installer will need to use. Also, marble often has natural variations in color and veining, which is part of its charm, but something to plan for in the layout. Finally, the subfloor is crucial; it needs to be perfectly flat and stable to prevent lippage and cracking. If you're tackling a big project, like a shower or a complex pattern, or if you're worried about staining or etching, bringing in a pro can really save you a headache down the line. They have the expertise to make sure your marble looks amazing and lasts.",
